WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.160
When it comes to the vast universe of&nbsp;
SCP, it’s not unusual to happen upon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.360
an entity from time to time that&nbsp;
you aren’t fully acquainted with.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.440
However, SCP-1000 goes by a name&nbsp;
you’re probably more familiar with:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.680
Bigfoot. That’s right, that bigfoot. The&nbsp;
Foundation keeps these creatures under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.600
wraps due to the fact that the simple sight&nbsp;
of them will infect you with a strange disease&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.040
that imparts the high probability&nbsp;
of you dropping dead instantly.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.160
Or does it?

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.880
The fact is, the Foundation is vastly overstating&nbsp;
the danger of these beasts for secretive reasons:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.520
what we refer to as bigfoots - or is it big&nbsp;
feet? - were actually once a hyper-advanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.760
nocturnal race that threatened to replace&nbsp;
humanity as the dominant species on earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.320
But a deal with a capricious forest&nbsp;
God put humanity back on top,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.080
and reduced SCP-1000 to a&nbsp;
tiny population of mere apes.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.600
The SCP Foundation doesn’t want YOU to&nbsp;
know any of this though, and so they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.240
made up the story about them&nbsp;
having looks that can kill.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:57.440
The good news for us is that it at least&nbsp;
seems that SCP-1000 doesn’t hold a grudge.

